      {
        "narration": "The survivors of this wreck were killed by each other. Not by thirst, not by the sea. By the man in charge.",
        "visual_query": "western australia coral reef islands",
        "visual_fallback": "coral reef"
      },
      {
        "narration": "On the fourth of June, 1629, the Dutch ship Batavia struck a reef off Western Australia with 341 people aboard.",
        "visual_query": "dutch east indiaman sailing ship",
        "visual_fallback": "sailing ship"
      },
      {
        "narration": "About three hundred reached the coral islands. The commander took a longboat and sailed for help, three thousand kilometres away.",
        "visual_query": "low barren coral island shoreline",
        "visual_fallback": "barren island"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Behind him, Jeronimus Cornelisz took charge. A bankrupt apothecary, a junior merchant, and now the only authority for hundreds of kilometres.",
        "visual_query": "17th century dutch merchant portrait",
        "visual_fallback": "old portrait"
      },
      {
        "narration": "He had roughly 125 people killed. Soldiers he had marooned fought back, and the rescue ship arrived mid-battle. Cornelisz was hanged.",
